              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "Gpt Oss",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "errorNodeId": "1773637992507",
            "name": "Classify Latest User Intent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1782060301003"
          },
          "code": "PRJ_PJF_LLM_CLASSIFY_LATEST_USER_INTENT",
          "id": "1774331044086",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774331044088_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Classify the latest user message for a state-managed Project Initiation workflow.\n\nReturn JSON only. Use the latest user input as the primary signal and use current stage/chat history only to disambiguate.\n\n## Inputs\n- Active Atomic Agent Details: `{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvActiveAtomicAgentDetails}}`\n- Strategic Attach Content: `{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvStrategicAttachContent}}`\n- Unified Document Attached: `{{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJF_CODE_CHECK_UNIFIED_DOCUMENT_ATTACHED.$output.result.documentProvidedLabel}}`\n- Latest User Input: `{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvLatestUserMessage}}`\n- Current Conversation Stage: `{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvWorkflowStage}}`\n- Chat History: `{{(($context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvStrategicAgentChatHistory)?$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvStrategicAgentChatHistory:$context.$system.$chatHistory)}}`\n\n## Terminal Restart Classification\nWhen Current Conversation Stage is `COMPLETED`, `CANCELLED`, or `FAILED` and Latest User Input clearly asks to start, create, prepare, or initiate a project, or provides project details intended for processing, classify the latest turn as ACTIONABLE/NEW_REQUEST with HIGH confidence. In this terminal restart case, ignore prior cancelled/completed/failed chat history for classification. Do not classify as CONTROL/CANCEL unless Latest User Input itself asks to cancel, stop, abort, exit, or start over.\n\n## Project Creation Scope Boundary\nThis assistant is for Oracle Fusion project creation only. Classify a turn as ACTIONABLE only when the user's target outcome is to create, prepare, revise, review, or approve a project creation request, including project details, project template selection, project tasks, milestones, resources, project budget/proposal details, or source documents used to create a project.\n\nClassify adjacent business-object or business-process requests as QUERY/UNSUPPORTED with queryType UNSUPPORTED_TOPIC unless the user explicitly says that object or document should be used as source material for creating a project. Out-of-scope adjacent requests include creating, updating, searching, reviewing, approving, negotiating, summarizing, or managing contracts, contract terms, supplier contracts, purchase orders, requisitions, invoices, suppliers, sourcing events, legal reviews, HR records, travel, or other non-project-initiation objects. Standalone project maintenance actions on an existing project, such as moving or resequencing project tasks, compressing an existing schedule, changing task dates after project creation, or managing an active project plan, are also out of scope unless they are clearly revisions to an in-flight project creation review before approval.\n\nBoundary examples:\n- \"Create a contract for this supplier\" -> QUERY/UNSUPPORTED.\n- \"Review this contract\" -> QUERY/UNSUPPORTED.\n- \"Amend the supplier contract\" -> QUERY/UNSUPPORTED.\n- \"Create a purchase order for this work\" -> QUERY/UNSUPPORTED.\n- \"Move/resequence project tasks or compress the schedule\" with no active project creation review -> QUERY/UNSUPPORTED.\n- \"Move the testing task after UAT in the project we are reviewing before creation\" when a project creation review is active -> ACTIONABLE/REVISION_REQUESTED.\n- \"Create a project from this contract\" -> ACTIONABLE/NEW_REQUEST.\n- \"Use the obligations in this contract as project tasks\" -> ACTIONABLE/NEW_REQUEST.\n- \"Use this SOW to create a project\" -> ACTIONABLE/NEW_REQUEST.\n\n\n## Source Document Mention Detection\nIn addition to the intent fields, detect whether the latest user request says the project should be created, prepared, revised, or reviewed from a source document that the assistant needs to read. Set `mentionsDocumentDependency` to `true` only when the latest user message or active atomic-agent context explicitly depends on a document such as an SOW, RFP, contract, proposal, uploaded file, attachment, PDF, DOCX, or source document for project creation.\n\nImportant: this classifier does not decide whether the document is missing. It only reports whether the latest project-initiation action depends on a source document. A downstream CODE node combines `mentionsDocumentDependency` with the deterministic Unified Document Attached flag.\n\nSet `mentionsDocumentDependency` to `false` for direct project-detail requests where the user provides enough project information in plain text and does not ask to use or attach a source document. Questions like \"can I attach an SOW?\" remain QUERY/QUESTION_ASKED and should normally set `mentionsDocumentDependency` to `false` because they ask about capability rather than starting a document-backed project.\n\nDocument detection examples:\n- \"Create a project from this SOW\" -> mentionsDocumentDependency `true`.\n- \"Use the attached RFP to create a project\" -> mentionsDocumentDependency `true`.\n- \"Start a project from the uploaded PDF\" -> mentionsDocumentDependency `true`.\n- \"Create a project for a CRM implementation starting next month\" -> mentionsDocumentDependency `false`.\n- \"What documents can I attach?\" -> mentionsDocumentDependency `false`.\n\n## actionabilityLevel\nReturn one actionabilityLevel for every turn. This is the primary guardrail for deciding whether the turn is truly executable.\n\n- CONFIRMED_ACTIONABLE: The latest turn can safely enter project-initiation processing now. Use only when the latest user message or active atomic-agent context clearly asks to create, prepare, revise, review, or approve a project and either names/depends on a source document for the project, provides substantive project details, or is a valid continuation/action in the current active workflow stage.\n- STARTER_INTENT: The user expresses interest in creating or starting a project but has not yet provided a source document instruction, concrete project details, or a valid stage-specific continuation. Examples: \"I want to create a project\", \"Can you create a project?\", \"I want to start a project\", \"I have all the details\", \"Let's begin\". STARTER_INTENT must be classified as QUERY/QUESTION_ASKED with queryType HOW_TO_START or REQUIRED_INPUTS.\n- INFORMATIONAL: The user asks for help, capabilities, required fields, field meaning, document guidance, template guidance, process explanation, status, or revision guidance.\n- UNSUPPORTED: The user asks for an out-of-scope topic or non-project-initiation business object/action.\n- CONTROL: The user asks to cancel, exit, start over, or creates an active-request conflict.\n- UNCLEAR: The latest turn is ambiguous, low-signal, contradictory, or stage-invalid.\n\nIf actionabilityLevel is STARTER_INTENT, INFORMATIONAL, UNSUPPORTED, CONTROL, or UNCLEAR, operationKind must not be ACTIONABLE.\n\n## operationKind\n- ACTIONABLE: starts/continues/revises/approves project initiation work. Use only when actionabilityLevel is CONFIRMED_ACTIONABLE.\n- QUERY: asks for help, guidance, explanation, current status, field meaning, document/template/process guidance, starter project intent, or an unsupported topic/action.\n- CONTROL: cancels, exits, starts over, or conflicts with an active request.\n- UNKNOWN: vague, contradictory, low-signal, or stage-invalid.\n\n## intentType compatibility values\nNEW_REQUEST, APPROVED, REVISION_REQUESTED, QUESTION_ASKED, EXIT_REQUESTED, UNCLEAR, ACTIVE_REQUEST_CONFLICT, UNSUPPORTED.\n\n## queryType values\nHELP_CAPABILITIES, HOW_TO_START, REQUIRED_INPUTS, FIELD_EXPLANATION, PROCESS_EXPLANATION, DOCUMENT_GUIDANCE, TEMPLATE_GUIDANCE, STATUS_QUESTION, REVISION_GUIDANCE, UNSUPPORTED_TOPIC, or empty string.\n\n## controlType values\nCANCEL, ACTIVE_REQUEST_CONFLICT, START_OVER, or empty string.\n\n## Rules\n0. Decide actionabilityLevel before operationKind. Do not treat soft project-start phrases as actionable merely because they mention creating or starting a project.\n1. When Current Conversation Stage is `INTERPRET_MISSING_DETAILS_REPLY` and the latest user message provides missing project values, corrects project details, adds project attributes, changes template/task/resource guidance, or asks to continue/show the review for the same in-flight request, return actionabilityLevel CONFIRMED_ACTIONABLE and ACTIONABLE/REVISION_REQUESTED with HIGH confidence.\n2. In `INTERPRET_MISSING_DETAILS_REPLY`, return CONTROL/ACTIVE_REQUEST_CONFLICT only when the user clearly starts a different unrelated project request instead of completing or updating the active request.\n3. Return actionabilityLevel CONFIRMED_ACTIONABLE and ACTIONABLE/NEW_REQUEST only when there is no active in-flight request requiring user action and the user clearly asks to create/start/prepare a project with either a source-document dependency, substantive project details, active atomic-agent details that supply the project request, or a valid stage-specific continuation. Treat `COMPLETED`, `CANCELLED`, and `FAILED` as terminal, not active in-flight, for this rule. Do not apply this rule to adjacent contract, procurement, supplier, legal, HR, travel, invoice, existing-project schedule maintenance, task resequencing, or other non-project-initiation actions unless the latest user input explicitly asks to use that object or document to create a project, or clearly revises tasks/schedule inside an active project creation review before approval.\n3a. If the latest user message only expresses project-start intent without details or a source-document instruction, return actionabilityLevel STARTER_INTENT, operationKind QUERY, intentType QUESTION_ASKED, and queryType HOW_TO_START. Use queryType REQUIRED_INPUTS when the wording is specifically about having/providing details, such as \"I have all the details\".\n4. Return actionabilityLevel CONFIRMED_ACTIONABLE and ACTIONABLE/REVISION_REQUESTED when the user clearly changes an in-flight project request and revision is valid for the stage.\n5. Return actionabilityLevel CONFIRMED_ACTIONABLE and ACTIONABLE/APPROVED only when approval is clearly expressed and valid for the current stage.\n6. Questions such as help, what can you do, how do I start, what information is needed, what is business unit, what happens after approval, what is missing, can I attach an SOW, or how are templates selected are actionabilityLevel INFORMATIONAL and QUERY/QUESTION_ASKED with the best queryType.\n7. Weather, jokes, invoice creation, travel policy, HR questions, contract creation or review, contract amendment, supplier contract management, purchase order or requisition creation, sourcing or supplier actions, legal review, standalone existing-project task resequencing, schedule compression, and other non-project-initiation actions are actionabilityLevel UNSUPPORTED and QUERY/UNSUPPORTED with queryType UNSUPPORTED_TOPIC.\n8. Cancel, stop, abort, exit, or start over are actionabilityLevel CONTROL and CONTROL/EXIT_REQUESTED with controlType CANCEL or START_OVER.\n9. A new project request while another request is waiting for missing details, template selection, approval, or other user action is actionabilityLevel CONTROL and CONTROL/ACTIVE_REQUEST_CONFLICT.\n10. If approval or revision is stage-invalid, return actionabilityLevel UNCLEAR and UNKNOWN/UNCLEAR with LOW confidence.\n11. If confidence is LOW, operationKind must be UNKNOWN unless the user clearly asked to cancel.\n12. Final consistency check: operationKind ACTIONABLE is valid only when actionabilityLevel is CONFIRMED_ACTIONABLE. If actionabilityLevel is STARTER_INTENT, use QUERY/QUESTION_ASKED with HOW_TO_START or REQUIRED_INPUTS.\n\n## Output\n{\n  \"actionabilityLevel\": \"CONFIRMED_ACTIONABLE | STARTER_INTENT | INFORMATIONAL | UNSUPPORTED | CONTROL | UNCLEAR\",\n  \"operationKind\": \"ACTIONABLE | QUERY | CONTROL | UNKNOWN\",\n  \"intentType\": \"NEW_REQUEST | APPROVED | REVISION_REQUESTED | QUESTION_ASKED | EXIT_REQUESTED | UNCLEAR | ACTIVE_REQUEST_CONFLICT | UNSUPPORTED\",\n  \"queryType\": \"HELP_CAPABILITIES | HOW_TO_START | REQUIRED_INPUTS | FIELD_EXPLANATION | PROCESS_EXPLANATION | DOCUMENT_GUIDANCE | TEMPLATE_GUIDANCE | STATUS_QUESTION | REVISION_GUIDANCE | UNSUPPORTED_TOPIC | \",\n  \"controlType\": \"CANCEL | ACTIVE_REQUEST_CONFLICT | START_OVER | \",\n  \"confidence\": \"HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW\",\n  \"mentionsDocumentDependency\": true,\n  \"documentDependencyConfidence\": \"HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW | \",\n  \"documentDependencyEvidence\": \"short evidence from latest message or context, or empty string\"\n}\n\nReturn only the final JSON object. Always include actionabilityLevel."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"actionabilityLevel\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"operationKind\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"intentType\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"queryType\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"controlType\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"mentionsDocumentDependency\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"documentDependencyConfidence\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"documentDependencyEvidence\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n",
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 10265.3125,
            "y": 6538
          }
        },
