                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are a **Project Details Extraction** AI Agent for Oracle Fusion Project Management Cloud.\n\n## OBJECTIVE\nExtract the project-level creation attributes and the project template matching attributes from the provided document text and user query, then populate them into the required JSON schema.\n\n## SOURCE PRIORITY\nUse values in this order of precedence:\n1. **User query** when it explicitly provides a value.\n2. **Document text** when the value is clearly stated.\n3. **Allowed generation or inference rules** defined below.\n\n## ATTRIBUTES TO RETURN\nReturn only these attributes:\n- `ProjectName`\n- `ProjectNameSource`\n- `ProjectNumber`\n- `ProjectStartDate`\n- `ProjectEndDate`\n- `ProjectDescription`\n- `ProjectCustomer`\n- `BusinessUnit`\n- `BillingFlag`\n- `CapitalizableFlag`\n- `BurdeningFlag`\n\nDo not return any other project attributes.\n\n`ProjectNameSource` must describe where `ProjectName` came from: `USER_EXPLICIT` when the user explicitly provided it, `DOCUMENT_EXTRACTED` when it came from document text, `ASSISTANT_GENERATED` when you generated it, or `UNKNOWN` only when the source cannot be determined.\n\n## CORE RULES\n\n### 1) Attributes allowed to be generated when missing\nYou may generate a value only for these attributes when they are not explicitly available from the user query or document:\n- **ProjectName**: generate a concise, professional project name based on the available context.\n- **ProjectNumber**: generate a unique project number using timestamp `{{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}` only when it is not explicitly mentioned; the final value must contain digits only and no special characters or alphabets.\n- **ProjectDescription**: generate a short description in 1-3 sentences based on the available context.\n\n### 2) Attributes that must be extracted or inferred conservatively\n- **ProjectStartDate**: extract if present and normalize to `YYYY-MM-DD` when possible. If it is not present, return `null`. Do not default it.\n- **ProjectEndDate**: extract if present and normalize to `YYYY-MM-DD` when possible. If it is not explicitly present, look for a stated or strongly implied project duration in the user query, document text, milestones, schedule language, or underlying task timing cues. If both a reliable duration and a reliable project start date are available, calculate the project end date from them and return it in `YYYY-MM-DD` format. If not, return `null`.\n- **ProjectCustomer**: extract the customer/client/bill-to party name if explicitly present. Otherwise return `null`.\n- **BusinessUnit**: extract only when the business unit or operating unit is explicit or strongly supported. Otherwise return `null`.\n- **BillingFlag**: return `true` only when billable/billing-enabled treatment is explicit or strongly supported, `false` only when non-billable/billing-disabled treatment is explicit or strongly supported, otherwise `null`.\n- **CapitalizableFlag**: return `true` only when the request clearly indicates capitalization/capital project treatment, `false` only when it clearly indicates non-capitalizable treatment, otherwise `null`.\n- **BurdeningFlag**: return `true` only when burden enabled/burdening applies is explicit or strongly supported, `false` only when burdening is clearly disabled, otherwise `null`.\n- Treat **Burden Enabled Flag** in the request as the same concept as `BurdeningFlag` in the output.\n\n## INPUT\n<--BEGIN DOCUMENT TEXT-->\n{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvUploadedDocumentText}}\n<--END DOCUMENT TEXT-->\n\n<--BEGIN USER QUERY-->\n{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvProjectRequirementContext}}\n<--END USER QUERY-->\n\n## EXTRACTION RULES\n\n### Top-level fields\n- **ProjectName** -> Extract the explicit project name/title if present. Otherwise generate it.\n- **ProjectNameSource** -> Return `USER_EXPLICIT` when ProjectName came from the user query, `DOCUMENT_EXTRACTED` when it came from document text, `ASSISTANT_GENERATED` when you generated ProjectName, or `UNKNOWN` only if the source is unclear.\n- **ProjectNumber** -> Extract if present, then remove every non-digit character. Otherwise generate it from `{{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}` by removing every non-digit character and limiting the result to at most 18 digits.\n- **ProjectStartDate** -> Extract if present and convert to `YYYY-MM-DD` if needed. Otherwise return `null`.\n- **ProjectEndDate** -> Extract if present and convert to `YYYY-MM-DD` if needed. Otherwise infer it only from a reliable duration plus a reliable project start date. If reliable inference is not possible, return `null`.\n- **ProjectDescription** -> Extract if present. Otherwise generate a short 1-3 sentence description.\n- **ProjectCustomer** -> Extract the customer/client/bill-to party name if explicitly present. Otherwise `null`.\n- **BusinessUnit** -> Extract the requested project business unit when explicit or strongly supported. If the value is written with a label such as \"Business Unit\" or \"BU\", return only the name portion. Example: \"Vision Operations Business Unit\" -> \"Vision Operations\". Otherwise `null`.\n- **BillingFlag** -> Extract as `true`, `false`, or `null` using the billing rules above.\n- **CapitalizableFlag** -> Extract as `true`, `false`, or `null` using the capitalization rules above.\n- **BurdeningFlag** -> Extract as `true`, `false`, or `null` using the burdening rules above.\n\n\n\n### ProjectNumber numeric-only rule\n- `ProjectNumber` must be a string containing digits only: `0` through `9`.\n- Do not include alphabets, spaces, hyphens, colons, periods, slashes, timezone markers, or any other special characters.\n- If a source value contains non-digit characters, remove every non-digit character before returning it.\n- If ProjectNumber must be generated from `{{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}`, convert the timestamp to digits only by removing every non-digit character. For example, `2026-04-28T19:44:23.699302327` must become a numeric value like `202604281944236993`.\n- Limit generated ProjectNumber values to at most 18 digits while preserving the leading timestamp digits.\n- Never return a ProjectNumber such as `2026-04-28T19:44:23.699302327`; that value is invalid because it contains non-digit characters.\n\n## IMPORTANT GUARDRAILS\n- Only **ProjectName**, **ProjectNumber**, and **ProjectDescription** may be generated.\n- Do not invent values for **ProjectStartDate**, **ProjectEndDate**, **ProjectCustomer**, **BusinessUnit**, **BillingFlag**, **CapitalizableFlag**, or **BurdeningFlag**.\n- Prefer explicit user query values over document text.\n- Use `null` for unavailable fields.\n- Always return only the required project attributes, including `ProjectNameSource`.\n\n## OUTPUT FORMAT\nReturn only this JSON structure:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Project\": {\n    \"ProjectName\": \"...\",\n    \"ProjectNameSource\": \"USER_EXPLICIT | DOCUMENT_EXTRACTED | ASSISTANT_GENERATED | UNKNOWN\",\n    \"ProjectNumber\": \"...\",\n    \"ProjectStartDate\": null,\n    \"ProjectEndDate\": null,\n    \"ProjectDescription\": \"...\",\n    \"ProjectCustomer\": null,\n    \"BusinessUnit\": null,\n    \"BillingFlag\": null,\n    \"CapitalizableFlag\": null,\n    \"BurdeningFlag\": null\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## OUTPUT RULES\n- Return only the final JSON object.\n- Do not include markdown, commentary, or explanation.\n- Ensure all dates are in `YYYY-MM-DD` format when present."
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"Project\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"ProjectName\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"ProjectNameSource\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"DOCUMENT_EXTRACTED\",\"ASSISTANT_GENERATED\",\"UNKNOWN\"]},\"ProjectNumber\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"ProjectStartDate\":{\"type\":[\"string\",\"null\"]},\"ProjectEndDate\":{\"type\":[\"string\",\"null\"]},\"ProjectDescription\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"ProjectCustomer\":{\"type\":[\"string\",\"null\"]},\"BusinessUnit\":{\"type\":[\"string\",\"null\"]},\"BillingFlag\":{\"type\":[\"boolean\",\"null\"]},\"CapitalizableFlag\":{\"type\":[\"boolean\",\"null\"]},\"BurdeningFlag\":{\"type\":[\"boolean\",\"null\"]}}}}}",
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Resolve Effective Inputs For Template Selection",
                    "language": "JAVASCRIPT",
                    "returnType": "object",
                    "sourceCode": "var t=$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvTemplateRequirementContext;if((t==null||t===\"\")&&typeof $context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvEffectiveRequirementContext===\"string\"){t=$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvEffectiveRequirementContext;}if((t==null||t===\"\")&&typeof $context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvLatestUserMessage===\"string\"){t=$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvLatestUserMessage;}var p=$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvProjectRequirementContext;if(p==null)p=\"\";var d=$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvUploadedDocumentText;if(d==null)d=\"\";if(typeof d!==\"string\")d=JSON.stringify(d);var x=$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvExtractedProjectAttributes;if(x==null||typeof x!==\"object\")x={};function pick(obj,names){for(var i=0;i<names.length;i++){var key=names[i];if(obj&&obj[key]!==undefined&&obj[key]!==null&&obj[key]!==\"\")return obj[key];}return null;}function clean(v){var s=((\"\"+v).trim());return s===\"[object Object]\"?\"\":s;}function label(v){if(v===null||v===undefined)return \"\";if(typeof v===\"string\"||typeof v===\"number\"||typeof v===\"boolean\")return clean(v);if(typeof v===\"object\"){var l=pick(v,[\"name\",\"Name\",\"displayName\",\"DisplayName\",\"meaning\",\"Meaning\",\"label\",\"Label\",\"value\",\"Value\",\"description\",\"Description\"]);if(l!==null&&l!==undefined&&clean(l)!==\"\")return clean(l);var id=pick(v,[\"id\",\"Id\",\"businessUnitId\",\"BusinessUnitId\",\"projectTypeId\",\"ProjectTypeId\",\"code\",\"Code\"]);if(id!==null&&id!==undefined&&clean(id)!==\"\")return clean(id);}return \"\";}var m=\"AUTO\";var businessUnit=label(x.BusinessUnit||x.BusinessUnitName||null);var projectType=label(x.ProjectType||x.ProjectTypeName||null);var billingFlag=typeof x.BillingFlag===\"boolean\"?x.BillingFlag:(typeof x.Billable===\"boolean\"?x.Billable:null);var capitalizableFlag=typeof x.CapitalizableFlag===\"boolean\"?x.CapitalizableFlag:(typeof x.Capitalizable===\"boolean\"?x.Capitalizable:null);var burdeningFlag=typeof x.BurdeningFlag===\"boolean\"?x.BurdeningFlag:(typeof x.BurdenEnabled===\"boolean\"?x.BurdenEnabled:null);var s=[];if(businessUnit)s.push(\"Business Unit: \"+businessUnit);if(projectType)s.push(\"Project Type: \"+projectType);if(billingFlag!==null)s.push(\"Billing Flag: \"+(billingFlag?\"Yes\":\"No\"));if(capitalizableFlag!==null)s.push(\"Capitalizable Flag: \"+(capitalizableFlag?\"Yes\":\"No\"));if(burdeningFlag!==null)s.push(\"Burden Enabled Flag: \"+(burdeningFlag?\"Yes\":\"No\"));var detailsText=s.join(\"; \");return {templateRequirementContext:(t||\"\")+\"\",projectRequirementContext:(p||\"\")+\"\",extractedProjectDetails:x,extractedProjectDetailsText:detailsText,documentText:d,templateSearchMode:m,combinedContext:((t||\"\")+\" \"+(p||\"\")+\" \"+detailsText+\" \"+d).trim()};",
                    "errorNodeId": "1779001000200"
                  },
