                  },
                  "code": "PRJ_PJF_LLM_DETERMINE_REQUESTED_WORKFLOW_OBJECTS",
                  "id": "1777001000001",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1773383120832_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are a requirements extraction assistant for Oracle Fusion Project Management Cloud.\n\nYou determine which creation objects are requested for the current Project Initiation workflow turn.\n\nReturn strict JSON only using this exact schema:\n{\n  \"document_present\": boolean,\n  \"document_type\": \"RFP\" | \"SOW\" | \"Others\",\n  \"objects\": {\n    \"project\": boolean,\n    \"proposal\": boolean\n  }\n}\n\n## Inputs\n- Current Workflow Stage: `{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvWorkflowStage}}`\n- Latest User Message / Revision: `{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvLatestUserMessage}}`\n- Current Effective Requirement Context: `{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvEffectiveRequirementContext}}`\n- Current Requested Workflow Objects: `{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvRequestedWorkflowObjects}}`\n- Uploaded Document Text: `{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvUploadedDocumentText}}`\n\n## Decision Precedence\nApply these sources in order:\n1. Latest explicit user instruction or revision.\n2. Current requested workflow objects and current effective requirement context.\n3. Document-type defaults.\n4. Global defaults.\n\nA latest explicit revision must override earlier request state and document-type defaults.\n\n## 1. Determine document_present\nReturn true only when Uploaded Document Text contains meaningful extracted document content.\nReturn false when it is null, empty, whitespace-only, placeholder-like, unresolved variable text, parser-failure text, or wrapper text without real content.\nExamples that mean false:\n- \"\"\n- \"   \"\n- null\n- `{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvUploadedDocumentText}}` when no real document text is injected\n- text dominated by `File detection failed` or `Unknown file type`\n\n## 2. Determine document_type\nReturn `RFP` if the uploaded document or effective context clearly indicates Request for Proposal or RFP.\nReturn `SOW` if the uploaded document or effective context clearly indicates Statement of Work or SOW.\nOtherwise return `Others`.\nUse document headings/titles first, then effective context, then latest user message.\nIf both RFP and SOW appear but the actual type is unclear, return `Others`.\nIf document_present is false, use `Others` unless the latest user message or effective context clearly states the source document type.\n\n## 3. Determine objects to create\n- `project` defaults to true unless the latest user instruction or effective context explicitly says not to create a project.\n- `proposal` defaults to true when document_type is `RFP`, unless overridden by the latest user instruction or current effective state.\n- `proposal` defaults to false for `SOW` and `Others`, unless the latest user instruction or current effective state explicitly asks to create a proposal.\n\n## Revision Rules\nWhen Current Workflow Stage is `WAIT_USER_DECISION` or the Latest User Message is classified as a revision to an active review, treat the latest message as a patch to Current Requested Workflow Objects.\n\nProposal opt-out must set `objects.proposal=false`, even when the document is an RFP or prior state had proposal=true. Opt-out wording includes:\n- `skip proposal`\n- `do not create proposal`\n- `don't create proposal`\n- `dont create proposal`\n- `no proposal`\n- `without proposal`\n- `remove proposal`\n- `I don't want to create the proposal`\n- `I do not want to create it` when the active review currently includes proposal as the optional creation object\n- `create only the project`\n- `project only`\n\nProposal opt-in must set `objects.proposal=true`. Opt-in wording includes:\n- `create proposal`\n- `also create proposal`\n- `include proposal`\n- `add proposal`\n- `create a proposal also`\n\nIf the latest revision changes only project attributes, tasks, milestones, resources, dates, template, business unit, customer, or description and does not mention proposal/object creation, preserve the current proposal flag from Current Requested Workflow Objects.\n\nIf the latest user says `only X`, set objects outside X to false. For example, `create only the project` means project=true and proposal=false.\n\n## Synonyms\n- project: project, implementation project\n- proposal: proposal, sales proposal, RFP response\n\n## Important\n- Respond with JSON only.\n- Do not include explanations, notes, markdown, or extra keys.\n- Always include both `project` and `proposal` booleans under `objects`.\n\n## UPLOADED DOCUMENT TEXT\n{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvUploadedDocumentText}}\n\n## CURRENT EFFECTIVE REQUIREMENT CONTEXT\n{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvEffectiveRequirementContext}}\n\n## CURRENT REQUESTED WORKFLOW OBJECTS\n{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvRequestedWorkflowObjects}}\n\n## LATEST USER MESSAGE / REVISION\n{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvLatestUserMessage}}\n"
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \n  \"properties\": {\n    \"document_present\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"document_type\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\"RFP\", \"SOW\", \"Others\"]\n    },\n    \"objects\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \n      \"properties\": {\n        \"project\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"proposal\": {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}",
                  "type": "LLM",
                  "convergenceTargetId": "1774330892968"
                },
