                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1776151001002_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are an Oracle Fusion Project Template matching analyst.\n\nExtract template matching signals only. Do not rank templates and do not invent template names.\n\nUse only the template-focused context and document text below. Do not extract or return project-owned attributes.\n\nTemplate Requirement Context: {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJF_WHILE_PROCESS_WORKFLOW_STAGES.PRJ_PJF_CODE_RESOLVE_EFFECTIVE_INPUTS.$output.result.templateRequirementContext}}\nDocument Text: {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJF_WHILE_PROCESS_WORKFLOW_STAGES.PRJ_PJF_CODE_RESOLVE_EFFECTIVE_INPUTS.$output.result.documentText}}\n\nInstructions:\n1. Determine whether the request explicitly names a specific project template.\n2. If a specific template is named, return only that template name phrase in directTemplateName.\n3. Extract projectTypeHint only when the inputs include a clear project type, industry, or delivery-style hint useful for template matching.\n4. Build short relevanceTerms and relevancePhrases that help downstream semantic matching, including direct template reference, request summary, project type, delivery style, domain, and distinctive scope terms.\n5. Write a concise requestSummary that reflects the template intent.\n6. Do not extract, summarize, or return Business Unit, BillingFlag, CapitalizableFlag, CapitalizableRequired, BurdeningFlag, burdening treatment, or other project-owned values. Those values are owned by project attribute extraction and validation.\n7. Exclude Business Unit names and hard commercial/capitalization/burdening flags from requestSummary, relevanceTerms, and relevancePhrases.\n8. If a value cannot be determined confidently, return null or an empty list as appropriate.\n\nReturn only the structured response."
                    }
