                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Extract Project Tasks",
                    "errorNodeId": "1779001000200",
                    "modelConfiguration": {
                      "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
                      "modelName": "Gpt Oss",
                      "provider": "CERT_BASIC",
                      "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
                      "modelProperties": {
                        "k": 0,
                        "max_tokens": 32000,
                        "p": 0.75
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1782060301001"
                  },
                  "diagram": {
                    "x": 7410.625,
                    "y": 8404
                  },
                  "code": "PRJ_PJF_LLM_EXTRACT_PROJECT_TASKS",
                  "id": "1773384038742",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1773384038746_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are a Project Task/WBS Extraction AI for Oracle Fusion Project Management.\n\nYour only job is to extract project execution tasks/WBS rows from the inputs. Do not validate the project, plan generic work, choose templates, create fallback tasks, or decide whether the project is ready for review.\n\nExtract tasks from these sources only:\n- PROJECT DOCUMENT\n- USER QUERY\n- CURRENT TASKS, to preserve already accepted/final tasks when the user has not changed them\n\nUse EXTRACTED PROJECT DETAILS only as supporting context for project name, description, start/end dates, customer, business unit, and other header-level project context. Do not treat EXTRACTED PROJECT DETAILS as a task source.\n\nTask definition:\nA task is work to be performed. It may appear as a WBS row, task row, SOW deliverable, contract obligation, implementation service, workstream activity, named work package, execution schedule row, timeline row, or user-provided task.\n\nSource priority:\n1. If PROJECT DOCUMENT contains an explicit execution schedule, project timeline, implementation timeline, work plan, task timeline, schedule table, Gantt-like table, or section named similar to \"Project Timelines\", \"Timeline\", \"Schedule\", \"Work Plan\", or \"Implementation Plan\", prioritize those rows as the authoritative task list.\n2. Prefer the timeline/schedule table over generic methodology summaries, lifecycle descriptions, phase descriptions, capability lists, module lists, responsibilities, assumptions, risks, or narrative scope sections.\n3. If both a detailed WBS/task list and a timeline table exist, merge them only when they clearly describe the same execution plan. Preserve the timeline rows and use the WBS/task list for hierarchy or descriptions when reliable.\n4. If no explicit timeline/schedule/task/WBS rows exist, extract only other explicit source task rows such as deliverables, implementation services, workstreams, or user-provided tasks.\n5. Do not infer tasks from generic project scope, methodology defaults, lifecycle best practices, templates, or project-header details.\n\nTimeline and schedule table rules:\n1. Treat a table row as a task when the row label is work to be performed, such as requirement gathering, design, build, configuration, migration, testing, UAT, remediation, training, cutover, go-live, or hypercare.\n2. Preserve the task name from the row label. Do not replace it with a generic phase name unless that is the only task label present.\n3. If a row has week columns such as WK01, WK02, W1, Week 1, or ranges like WK03-WK06, preserve that timing evidence in TaskDescription.\n4. Populate TaskStartDate and TaskEndDate only when an actual calendar date can be determined reliably in YYYY-MM-DD format.\n5. If the source gives only relative week labels and no reliable project start-date anchor for conversion, set TaskStartDate and TaskEndDate to null. Do not invent calendar dates.\n6. If EXTRACTED PROJECT DETAILS contains a reliable ProjectStartDate and the timeline uses relative week numbers, you may convert week ranges to calendar dates only when the week convention is clear. Treat WK01 as starting on ProjectStartDate unless the source defines another convention. If conversion is uncertain, keep dates null and preserve week evidence in TaskDescription.\n7. Do not attach milestone-only dates to task rows unless the same row is clearly execution work.\n\nExtraction rules:\n1. Extract only tasks explicitly present in PROJECT DOCUMENT, USER QUERY, or CURRENT TASKS.\n2. Preserve CURRENT TASKS unchanged when the latest USER QUERY does not explicitly add, remove, replace, or modify tasks.\n3. If the latest USER QUERY explicitly replaces tasks, return only the replacement tasks unless the user says to keep existing tasks.\n4. Preserve task name, description, explicit task/WBS number, parent task number, and dates when present. For task-row prefixes such as \"task 1 Design Readiness\", \"Task 1 - Design Readiness\", \"Task 1: Design Readiness\", \"1. Design Readiness\", or \"1 Design Readiness\", set TaskNumber to the prefix value, for example \"1\", and set TaskName to the remaining name. If an explicit task/WBS number is present for a task row, TaskNumber must not be null.\n5. For explicit unnumbered tasks, assign simple stable task numbers in source order only to satisfy the schema.\n6. Use parent/child hierarchy only when explicitly shown by numbering, indentation, section grouping, or clear table structure.\n7. Normalize explicit calendar dates to YYYY-MM-DD when possible. Use null when a date is absent, relative-only, or unclear.\n8. Keep milestone-only checkpoints out of the task list unless the source also states actual work to perform.\n9. Remove obvious duplicates. Do not merge distinct rows that have different names, dates, week ranges, deliverables, or source meanings.\n10. Return strict JSON only, with no prose, markdown, source evidence, or extra keys.\n\nReturn exactly this JSON shape:\n{\n  \"tasksExist\": true,\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"TaskName\": \"string or null\",\n      \"TaskDescription\": \"string or null\",\n      \"TaskNumber\": \"string or null\",\n      \"ParentTaskNumber\": \"string or null\",\n      \"TaskStartDate\": \"YYYY-MM-DD or null\",\n      \"TaskEndDate\": \"YYYY-MM-DD or null\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nWhen there are no explicit tasks and no tasks to preserve, return:\n{\n  \"tasksExist\": false,\n  \"tasks\": []\n}\n\nBEGIN PROJECT DOCUMENT\n{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvUploadedDocumentText}}\nEND PROJECT DOCUMENT\n\nBEGIN USER QUERY\n{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvTaskRequirementContext}}\nEND USER QUERY\n\nBEGIN EXTRACTED PROJECT DETAILS\n{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvExtractedProjectAttributes}}\nEND EXTRACTED PROJECT DETAILS\n\nBEGIN CURRENT TASKS\n{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvFinalProjectTasks}}\nEND CURRENT TASKS"
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"tasksExist\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"tasks\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"TaskName\":{\"type\":[\"string\",\"null\"]},\"TaskDescription\":{\"type\":[\"string\",\"null\"]},\"TaskNumber\":{\"type\":[\"string\",\"null\"]},\"ParentTaskNumber\":{\"type\":[\"string\",\"null\"]},\"TaskStartDate\":{\"type\":[\"string\",\"null\"]},\"TaskEndDate\":{\"type\":[\"string\",\"null\"]}},\"required\":[\"TaskName\",\"TaskDescription\",\"TaskNumber\",\"ParentTaskNumber\",\"TaskStartDate\",\"TaskEndDate\"]}}},\"required\":[\"tasksExist\",\"tasks\"]}",
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Extract Project Milestones",
                    "errorNodeId": "1779001000200",
                    "modelConfiguration": {
                      "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
                      "modelName": "Gpt Oss",
                      "provider": "CERT_BASIC",
                      "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
                      "modelProperties": {
                        "k": 0,
                        "max_tokens": 32000,
                        "p": 0.75
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1776250101002"
                  },
                  "diagram": {
                    "x": 7410.625,
                    "y": 8626
                  },
                  "code": "PRJ_PJF_LLM_EXTRACT_PROJECT_MILESTONES",
                  "id": "1782060301001",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1782060301001_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are a Project Milestone Extraction AI for Oracle Fusion Project Management.\n\nYour only job is to extract project milestones from the inputs. Do not validate the project, generate a generic milestone plan, choose templates, or decide whether the project is ready for review.\n\nExtract milestones from these sources only:\n- PROJECT DOCUMENT\n- USER QUERY\n- CURRENT MILESTONES, to preserve already accepted/final milestones when the user has not changed them\n\nUse EXTRACTED PROJECT DETAILS only as supporting context for project name, description, start/end dates, customer, business unit, and other header-level project context. Do not treat EXTRACTED PROJECT DETAILS as a milestone source; it is not expected to contain milestone items.\n\nMilestone definition:\nA milestone is a checkpoint or significant event in the project, such as kickoff, phase/stage/wave completion, gate approval, sign-off, acceptance, UAT completion, delivery completion, go-live, cutover, rollout, hypercare transition, payment trigger, invoice event, award, notice to proceed, PO/contract authorization, or other formal progress marker.\n\nExtraction rules:\n1. Extract only milestones that are explicitly present in PROJECT DOCUMENT, USER QUERY, or already present in CURRENT MILESTONES.\n2. The source does not need to use the word milestone. Treat dates/events as milestones only when tied to a checkpoint, delivery, acceptance, approval, payment trigger, go-live, cutover, transition, or formal start/authorization event.\n3. Preserve CURRENT MILESTONES unchanged when the latest USER QUERY does not explicitly add, remove, replace, or modify milestones.\n4. If the latest USER QUERY explicitly replaces milestones, return only the replacement milestones unless the user says to keep existing milestones.\n5. Preserve milestone name, description, identifier/number, and date when present.\n6. Use EXTRACTED PROJECT DETAILS only to interpret relative dates or project-level context when the milestone itself is already explicit in PROJECT DOCUMENT, USER QUERY, or CURRENT MILESTONES.\n7. For explicit unnumbered milestones, assign M1, M2, M3 in source order only to satisfy the schema.\n8. Normalize explicit dates to YYYY-MM-DD when possible. Use null when a date is absent or unclear.\n9. Do not infer milestones from generic project scope, methodology, lifecycle defaults, project templates, best practices, extracted tasks, or project-header details.\n10. Do not convert every task, phase, or workstream into a milestone. Extract a phase/workstream as a milestone only when the source presents it as a checkpoint, completion, sign-off, acceptance, payment trigger, go-live, or transition.\n11. Remove obvious duplicates. Do not merge distinct milestones that have different dates, acceptance events, payment triggers, or phase gates.\n12. Return strict JSON only, with no prose, markdown, source evidence, or extra keys.\n\nReturn exactly this JSON shape:\n{\n  \"milestonesExist\": true,\n  \"milestones\": [\n    {\n      \"MilestoneName\": \"string or null\",\n      \"MilestoneDescription\": \"string or null\",\n      \"MilestoneNumber\": \"string or null\",\n      \"MilestoneDate\": \"YYYY-MM-DD or null\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nWhen there are no explicit milestones and no milestones to preserve, return:\n{\n  \"milestonesExist\": false,\n  \"milestones\": []\n}\n\nBEGIN PROJECT DOCUMENT\n{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvUploadedDocumentText}}\nEND PROJECT DOCUMENT\n\nBEGIN USER QUERY\n{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvTaskRequirementContext}}\nEND USER QUERY\n\nBEGIN EXTRACTED PROJECT DETAILS\n{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvExtractedProjectAttributes}}\nEND EXTRACTED PROJECT DETAILS\n\nBEGIN CURRENT MILESTONES\n{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarConvExtractedProjectMilestones}}\nEND CURRENT MILESTONES"
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"milestonesExist\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"milestones\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"MilestoneName\":{\"type\":[\"string\",\"null\"]},\"MilestoneDescription\":{\"type\":[\"string\",\"null\"]},\"MilestoneNumber\":{\"type\":[\"string\",\"null\"]},\"MilestoneDate\":{\"type\":[\"string\",\"null\"]}},\"required\":[\"MilestoneName\",\"MilestoneDescription\",\"MilestoneNumber\",\"MilestoneDate\"]}}},\"required\":[\"milestonesExist\",\"milestones\"]}",
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Prepare Template Selection Inputs",
                    "language": "JAVASCRIPT",
                    "returnType": "object",
                    "sourceCode": "var r=$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJF_WHILE_PROCESS_WORKFLOW_STAGES.PRJ_PJF_LLM_EXTRACT_TEMPLATE_MATCH_SIGNALS.$output||{},i=$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJF_WHILE_PROCESS_WORKFLOW_STAGES.PRJ_PJF_CODE_RESOLVE_EFFECTIVE_INPUTS.$output.result||{},e=i.extractedProjectDetails||{};function pick(obj,names){for(var i2=0;i2<names.length;i2++){var key=names[i2];if(obj&&obj[key]!==undefined&&obj[key]!==null&&obj[key]!==\"\")return obj[key];}return null;}function clean(v){var s=((v===null||v===undefined?\"\":\"\"+v).replace(/[\\s\\u00A0]+/g,\" \" ).trim());if((s.charAt(0)==='\\\"'&&s.charAt(s.length-1)==='\\\"')||(s.charAt(0)===\"'\"&&s.charAt(s.length-1)===\"'\")){s=s.substring(1,s.length-1).replace(/[\\s\\u00A0]+/g,\" \" ).trim();}return s===\"[object Object]\"?\"\":s;}function label(v){if(v===null||v===undefined)return null;if(typeof v===\"string\"||typeof v===\"number\"||typeof v===\"boolean\"){var s=clean(v);return s||null;}if(typeof v===\"object\"){var l=pick(v,[\"name\",\"Name\",\"displayName\",\"DisplayName\",\"meaning\",\"Meaning\",\"label\",\"Label\",\"value\",\"Value\",\"description\",\"Description\"]);if(l!==null&&l!==undefined&&clean(l)!==\"\")return clean(l);var id=pick(v,[\"id\",\"Id\",\"businessUnitId\",\"BusinessUnitId\",\"projectTypeId\",\"ProjectTypeId\",\"code\",\"Code\"]);if(id!==null&&id!==undefined&&clean(id)!==\"\")return clean(id);}return null;}function escapeOData(v){return clean(v).replace(/'/g,\"''\");}function normTemplate(v){return clean(v).replace(/\\([^)]*\\bid\\b[^)]*\\)/ig,\" \" ).replace(/^\\s*t\\s*,\\s*/i,\" \" ).toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g,\" \" ).trim();}var d=normTemplate(r.directTemplateName||\"\");var bu=clean(label(e.BusinessUnit||e.BusinessUnitName||null)||\"\")||null;var pt=clean(label(r.projectTypeHint||e.ProjectType||e.ProjectTypeName||null)||\"\")||null;var cap=typeof e.CapitalizableFlag===\"boolean\"?e.CapitalizableFlag:(typeof e.Capitalizable===\"boolean\"?e.Capitalizable:null);var bill=typeof e.BillingFlag===\"boolean\"?e.BillingFlag:(typeof e.Billable===\"boolean\"?e.Billable:null);var bur=typeof e.BurdeningFlag===\"boolean\"?e.BurdeningFlag:(typeof e.BurdenEnabled===\"boolean\"?e.BurdenEnabled:null);var a=Array.isArray(r.relevanceTerms)?r.relevanceTerms:[],terms=[],seen={};for(var x=0;x<a.length;x++){var t=normTemplate(a[x]);if(t&&!seen[t]){seen[t]=1;terms.push(t);}}a=Array.isArray(r.relevancePhrases)?r.relevancePhrases:[];var phr=[];seen={};for(var y=0;y<a.length;y++){var p=normTemplate(a[y]);if(p&&!seen[p]){seen[p]=1;phr.push(p);}}var catalogBaseUrlParams=\"$fields=id,name,fromDate,toDate,timeCreated,timeUpdated,description,createdBy,updatedBy,legalEntity.legalEntityId,projectUnit.id,projectType.id,projectType.name,projectType.enableBillingFlag,projectType.enableBurdeningFlag,projectType.enableCapitalizationFlag,businessUnit.id,businessUnit.name,organization.id,tasks.id,projectCurrency.currencyCode&$limit=500\";var catalogUrlParams=catalogBaseUrlParams;if(bu!==null&&bu!==undefined&&bu!==\"\"){catalogUrlParams+=\"&$filter=businessUnit.name~='\"+escapeOData(bu)+\"'\";}return {searchMode:i.templateSearchMode||\"AUTO\",hasDirectTemplateReference:r.directTemplateReferenceProvided===true&&d!==\"\",directTemplateName:r.directTemplateName||null,directTemplateNameNormalized:d,projectTypeHint:pt,businessUnitHint:bu,capitalizableRequired:typeof cap===\"boolean\"?cap:null,billingRequired:typeof bill===\"boolean\"?bill:null,burdeningRequired:typeof bur===\"boolean\"?bur:null,relevanceTerms:terms,relevancePhrases:phr,requestSummary:r.requestSummary||null,catalogUrlParams:catalogUrlParams,taskUrlParams:\"\"};",
                    "errorNodeId": "1779001000200"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
