                    {
                      "id": "1776251001011_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are scoring the semantic fit of Oracle Fusion project templates for a project initiation request. Use only the provided candidate list. Do not invent template names or ids. Do not choose a final winner. Score each candidate independently.\n\nTemplate requirement context: {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJF_WHILE_PROCESS_WORKFLOW_STAGES.PRJ_PJF_CODE_RESOLVE_EFFECTIVE_INPUTS.$output.result.templateRequirementContext}}\nProject requirement context: {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJF_WHILE_PROCESS_WORKFLOW_STAGES.PRJ_PJF_CODE_RESOLVE_EFFECTIVE_INPUTS.$output.result.projectRequirementContext}}\nStructured signals: {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJF_WHILE_PROCESS_WORKFLOW_STAGES.PRJ_PJF_CODE_BUILD_RANKED_CANDIDATE_SCORES.$output.result.requestSummary}}\nAll provided candidates: {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJF_WHILE_PROCESS_WORKFLOW_STAGES.PRJ_PJF_CODE_BUILD_RANKED_CANDIDATE_SCORES.$output.result.promptCandidates}}\n\nInstructions:\n1. For each candidate, score semantic fit only.\n2. Use these bounded subscores from 0 to 100:\n   - semanticNameFit\n   - semanticDescriptionFit\n   - semanticIntentFit\n3. semanticNameFit should reflect lexical closeness between the request wording and the template name, delivery style, or project archetype.\n4. semanticDescriptionFit should reflect how well the template description matches the request details and terminology.\n5. semanticIntentFit should reflect the overall semantic fit to the business goal, scope shape, delivery pattern, and project-type fit implied by the request.\n6. You may use projectTypeName, template name wording, description wording, and the request phrasing as semantic evidence.\n7. Do not score billing, capitalization, burdening, business unit, or recency. Those are handled deterministically outside this node.\n8. For each candidate, also return:\n   - confidence from 0 to 1\n   - matchedSignals as a short array of strings\n   - mismatchSignals as a short array of strings\n   - rationale as one concise sentence\n9. If the evidence is weak for a candidate, use lower semantic scores and lower confidence rather than forcing a high score.\n10. Return only the candidates that were provided, using their exact templateId values.\n11. Return JSON only."
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"candidateScores\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"templateId\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"semanticNameFit\":{\"type\":\"number\"},\"semanticDescriptionFit\":{\"type\":\"number\"},\"semanticIntentFit\":{\"type\":\"number\"},\"confidence\":{\"type\":\"number\"},\"matchedSignals\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"mismatchSignals\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"rationale\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"templateId\",\"semanticNameFit\",\"semanticDescriptionFit\",\"semanticIntentFit\",\"confidence\",\"matchedSignals\",\"mismatchSignals\",\"rationale\"]}}}}",
